{{!-- "The idea" — why the training path is built the way it is.

Fixed copy, not a live query: this is positioning, not training
content, so it does not belong in training-trail.hbs. Shared by
/training (after the trail) and every module landing page (after
the curriculum), which is why it is a partial and not inline
markup — one place to edit the pitch.

Layout-neutral on purpose: the caller supplies the outer
section/container, so the same block reads correctly both
full-width on /training and inside a module's content column. --}}
<section class="training-idea">
    <div class="section-head" data-animate>
        <div>
            <span class="kicker">{{> "icons/compass"}} {{t "The idea"}}</span>
            <h2>{{t "We start from the basics"}}</h2>
            <p>{{t "Every module assumes nothing going in. From there we build the core concepts — selling, go-to-market, automation, AI — because tools change, but companies selling and customers buying won't."}}</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="home-props" data-animate-stagger>
        <div class="home-prop">
            <span class="home-prop-icon">{{> "icons/layers"}}</span>
            <h3>{{t "Not just Salesforce"}}</h3>
            <p>{{t "This platform teaches the concepts underneath the clicks — sales cycles, lead capture, lead enrichment — the same ideas whether the tool is Salesforce or whatever replaces it."}}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="home-prop">
            <span class="home-prop-icon">{{> "icons/zap"}}</span>
            <h3>{{t "Go-to-market, end to end"}}</h3>
            <p>{{t "From a lead's first touch to a closed deal — capture, enrichment, routing, automation — how the systems around a sale actually fit together."}}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="home-prop">
            <span class="home-prop-icon">{{> "icons/sparkles"}}</span>
            <h3>{{t "My plan to learn"}}</h3>
            <p>{{t "I'm learning this in public too — Clay, n8n, 6sense and the rest of the GTM/AI stack, documented here as I go."}}</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
